{"status":"recommendation","recommendation":{"stack":"Next.js (TypeScript) + Prisma + PostgreSQL + Vitest + Playwright","reasons":["You and your partner both log in and share the same data, so it needs a real server-side database from the start — Next.js gives you the app and the API in one project, with Prisma/Postgres as the shared store","Your core flow is CSV in → categorised → 'where my money goes', which is import-parse-persist-render — exactly the full-stack path Next.js handles end to end","Vitest covers the parse/categorise logic fast, and Playwright can watch the real 'import one CSV row and see it on screen' slice run in a browser — a human can literally watch the test go green","It's one TypeScript codebase, so budgets, charts and bank sync later slot in without bolting a backend on afterwards"],"slice":"importing one CSV row and showing it on screen","deferred":["Budgets against categories","Charts / spending visualisations","Bank sync","Real categorisation rules (beyond one hardcoded rule for the slice)","Multi-user auth and account management polish","CSV import of multiple rows / full statements"]}}

